The original problem involves Nancy starting with 80 files on her computer. She deletes 31 files, leaving her with $80 - 31 = 49$ files. These remaining files are then distributed into folders, with each folder containing 7 files. To find the number of folders, divide the remaining files by the number of files per folder:

$$
\frac{49}{7} = 7
$$

Thus, Nancy ends up with $\boxed{7}$ folders.  
