   $$
   2 \text{ shelves} \times 6 \text{ books per shelf} = 12 \text{ books}
   $$

2. Calculate the number of picture books:
   $$
   6 \text{ shelves} \times 6 \text{ books per shelf} = 36 \text{ books}
   $$

3. Add the number of mystery and picture books together:
   $$
   12 \text{ books} + 36 \text{ books} = 48 \text{ books}
   $$

Thus, Nancy has a total of $\boxed{48}$ books. 

