$$
46 - 10 = 36
$$

So, Oliver has 36 books to put away. The problem states that he can fit 4 books on each shelf. To find out how many shelves he needs, we divide the total number of books by the number of books per shelf:

$$
36 \div 4 = 9
$$

Since the division is exact (no remainder), Oliver will need exactly **9 shelves**.

$$
\boxed{9}
$$

